                        <cell>1.8%</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Minority</cell>
                        <cell>0.9%</cell>
                        <cell>2.4%</cell>
                        <cell>3.0%</cell>
                        <cell>1.6%</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>Total Employment</cell>
                        <cell>a<anchor n="4" xml:id="d210-f4"/>
                        </cell>
                        <cell>1.0%</cell>
                        <cell>2.8%</cell>
                        <cell>a<anchor n="5" xml:id="d210-f5"/>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">REPRESENTATION BY GRADE LEVEL</p>
                <p>As indicated in the report to the President, we believe the level of jobs held by
                    women and minorities to be a better measure of their advancement (and therefore
                    of the effectiveness of affirmative action efforts) than overall representation.
                    For your agency, these representation levels are as follows:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">Distribution of Women and Minorities</p>
                <p rendition="#center">by General Schedule Grade</p>
                <p rendition="#center">Full Time Permanent Employment Nov. 30, 1977</p>
                <p rendition="#center">GENERAL SCHEDULE &amp; EQUIVALENT<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d210-f6"/>
                </p>
                <table cols="3">
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
